subsection:: See also
link::Guides/Stochastica-GENDY::, link::Guides/Stochastica::, link::Classes/Gendy1977::

classmethods::
method:: ar
argument:: ampDist
Amplitude innovation law: 0 uniform, 1 truncated Cauchy, 2 truncated logistic, 3 truncated hyperbolic secant, 4 arcsine, 5 mapped truncated exponential. Integer clipped to 0..5; see the GENDY guide for quantiles. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: durDist
Duration innovation law, using the same IDs as ampDist. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: ampShape
Amplitude distribution shape, clipped to 0.0001..1. Uniform ignores it. The transforms are modern normalized quantiles; sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: durShape
Duration distribution shape, clipped to 0.0001..1; sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: minFreq
Lower frequency bound in Hz, giving the longest segment fs/(numPoints*minFreq). Bounds are sorted and clipped to 0.001..fs/numPoints. Sampled at cycle entry; this is not fixed-pitch normalization.
argument:: maxFreq
Upper frequency bound in Hz, giving the shortest segment fs/(numPoints*maxFreq). Equal frequency bounds fix segment duration. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: ampPrimaryRange
Primary amplitude half-width as a ratio of the full secondary interval width 2, clipped to 0..1. Zero sets the primary increment to zero and freezes the secondary amplitude. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: durPrimaryRatio
Primary duration half-width divided by the secondary duration interval width, clipped to 0..1. Zero freezes duration. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: ampPrimaryStep
Innovation size as a fraction of the full primary amplitude interval, clipped to 0..1. Zero freezes the primary walk, whose retained position can still move the secondary walk. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: durPrimaryStep
Innovation size as a fraction of the full primary duration interval, clipped to 0..1. Zero holds the primary position, not necessarily the duration. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: numPoints
Construction-time number of remembered breakpoints, clipped to 2..64 and truncated to an integer. Recreate the Synth to change it.
argument:: reset
Nonpositive-to-positive edge rewinds the original local seed, all point states and scheduler state. The reset sample equals the first sample of a fresh instance; a held positive value does not keep resetting. Audio-rate reset is supported.
argument:: seed
Construction-time local PCG32 seed. Nonzero seeds repeat for identical inputs and rate. Zero derives a seed from the parent Synth RNG once; reset reuses it. Cross-platform last-bit differences are possible.
returns::
One audio-rate waveform, bounded to -1..1 before external scaling. No control-rate constructor is provided.

examples::
subsection:: Minimal example
code::
(
{ LeakDC.ar(Gendy1991.ar(seed: 1991)) ! 2 * 0.07 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Motion near reflecting barriers
Small primary innovations change the persistent direction slowly; low range ratios retain more audible pitch structure.
code::
(
{
    var x = Gendy1991.ar(minFreq: 90, maxFreq: 240, ampPrimaryRange: 0.03,
        durPrimaryRatio: 0.015, ampPrimaryStep: 0.025, durPrimaryStep: 0.025, seed: 67);
    LeakDC.ar(x) ! 2 * 0.07 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::
